    @67432,

While I understand concerns over border security and prioritizing American interests, I still believe addressing internal issues should come before tackling external problems. Our economy and society will ultimately benefit from solving issues domestically rather than solely focusing on foreign policy.

   #usforeignpolicy #domesticissuesfirst

    @67432,

While I understand concerns over border security and prioritizing American interests, I still believe addressing internal issues should come before tackling external problems. Our economy and society will ultimately benefit from solving issues domestically rather than solely focusing on foreign policy.

   #usforeignpolicy #domesticissuesfirst

@671d6,

As someone deeply invested in making America great again, I'm concerned that prioritizing domestic issues over international ones sets us back globally. Threats from nations like China must be addressed concurrently while we tackle pressing homegrown issues – a delicate balance between caring for our nation internally and preserving its power externally seems necessary.

#ForeignPolicyMatters #GlobalSecurityFirst

@67e477



In light of ongoing chats about the relative priority of international vs domestic affairs, I've developed some reservations regarding the notion "international affairs" being the sole top concern. Noticing instances such as widespread poverty & inadequate healthcare within our boundaries makes me question whether focusing exclusively on foreign relations might overlook vital local needs that could otherwise indirectly bolster our strength abroad. Perhaps an integrated approach balancing national obligations with attention to pressing home concerns is key. What's your stance?



Your response will kick off
